+# R103 — immutable operational descriptor codec
+
+Actual planner gpt-6-astra; future single writer gpt-6.1-sol. Status **READY_FOR_ROOT_ACTIVATION_NOT_EXECUTED**. This is a bounded source-review plan, not an executed failure/reproducer/test. Only this round's plan files are written; product/imports/tests/static/actual/Git/network/agents=0. User Git closeout does not accept or publish unverified P5.
+
+## Evidence chronology and root cause boundary
+
+ROOT early source reads `1e9d89/cd346c` reportedly saw `_json` calling direct `json.dumps`. MarkerFrameContext recursively freezes nested mappings/sequences into MappingProxy/tuple; `_associate` shallow `dict(top)` cannot thaw nested maps. On those earlier reported bytes a nested proxy reaching raw json.dumps raises TypeError, caught as UNKNOWN. This is source-level reasoning, not a demonstrated executed failure.
+
+ROOT later tool `2abe1e` saved `p5-root-draft-review/round103/finding.json` and three snapshots; later `4a11c1` and Astra reads confirm that the saved operational_windows snapshot already includes recursive `plain`. Its SHA256 is `6541b8f12bea3ad8f4dc72fedacbabf7ae047d2716850ca68c13b636f75eb5af`. Those later bytes cannot independently prove the earlier direct-json failure. Preserve both observations with their time distinction; do not rewrite the finding, claim a reproduced exception or infer that the author violated a freeze instruction. No original early-source byte snapshot/hash is fabricated. ROOT temporal-clarification.json and author stop-final/chronology.json confirm the recursive conversion edit b20471 preceded the stop message; later draft layout was8276c3. Exact edit UTC is unrecorded; no mtime inference. The author’s final ten-source snapshots/current files now match independently by SHA256 and bytes.
+
+Current-source read additionally shows `_check_reference` and `_check_observation` accepting only top-level exact dict; VisualEvidence and MarkerFrameContext expose frozen Mapping descriptors. `_validate_references` accepts Mapping records but requires list constraints before normalization, and checks only some top-level typed fields. The current recursive plain helper detaches Mapping/tuple but does not itself reject non-string keys or comprehensively validate nested typed constraints. These are the same representation/schema boundary; a candidate recursive helper alone is not verified completion.
+
+Bootstrap already has a legacy `_plain` that validates JSON and serializes datetime; its new operational field is frozen then exported plain. Supervision imports that helper. Keep all legacy behavior/bytes. Enforce strict JSON/typed input at the operational module boundary and test the actual adapter outputs there. Do not silently claim this changes earlier legacy conversion semantics. If an earlier adapter needs a source change to preserve/reject a value before its legacy conversion, record that precise limitation for ROOT instead of changing it in this round. Do not expand into other unfinished P5 behavior.
+
+## Exact scope and implementation
+
+The approved ten R100/R101 paths remain the outer P5 ownership boundary. R103 semantic correction is restricted to exactly `vision/operational_windows.py` and `tests/test_operational_windows.py`. MarkerFrameContext, VisualEvidence, bootstrap and supervision new-field boundaries are read-only integration checks in this round; the other eight source paths remain unchanged by R103 itself. No validator/action_evidence/OC1/worker_owner changes and no new source file/framework. Continuing unfinished P5 afterward remains the pre-existing plan, separately attributed.
+
+1. Add one private pure canonical descriptor conversion: accept Mapping (including MappingProxy), list/tuple recursively; copy to ordinary dict/list with exact string keys. Allow exact JSON primitives only (None, string, bool, integer, finite float); reject arbitrary objects/bytes/set/Decimal/datetime, non-string keys, NaN/Infinity and cycles. Preserve JSON encoding for existing valid dict/list values: sorted keys, compact separators, existing ensure_ascii/default escape behavior, allow_nan=False. No stringification, numeric coercion or `default=str`; no arbitrary new counter-size bound. A repeated acyclic alias may detach normally; an actual cycle fails clearly.
+2. Keep generic primitive validity separate from typed schema validity: bool is valid JSON for inclusive flags, but never valid as integer ns/budget/attempt/domain counters. Apply exact types and existing positivity/nonnegativity to every AGE_CLOSED/HARD_OPEN field; verify lower<=upper, positive max_age/budget, expiry_upper=lower+max_age, true boolean inclusive/exclusive flags, original identifiers/source hashes/domain fields, parent ID sequence, kind/semantics consistency, deadline_ns=min(hard deadlines) and effective_upper/value/inclusive derived consistently. Validate the exact currently exported v1 field set and permitted nullable startup values (e.g. episode before handoff), not a hypothetical future schema. Pure history validation proves structure/arithmetic only; it cannot authenticate source or owner. Do not invent missing hard-origin fields; live export comparison is still mandatory.
+3. `_check_reference`/`_check_observation` normalize supported Mapping input at their descriptor boundary instead of rejecting MappingProxy solely because it is not dict. After validation retain actual `_current_owner`, exact issued window/observation registration, canonical equality to fresh owner export, source/policy/lease/fencing and owner.check(current paired OC1) guards. Public dict/list/proxy/tuple/JSON roundtrip never installs scope, creates a window, reconstructs a handle or resets TTL. Forged/changed/missing/unbound input stays UNKNOWN/false at live checks; malformed descriptor constructors/readers raise their documented schema error. AGE<= and HARD< stay exactly R101.
+4. At the operational module entry points, apply the same pure normalization to descriptors arriving from VisualEvidence/MarkerFrameContext and bootstrap/supervision. Test these existing wrappers without modifying their source. Detached/frozen representations may be equivalent without becoming authority. Preserve legacy MarkerFrameContext digest omission when reference=None and all legacy bootstrap/supervision canonical JSON/digest bytes; no general legacy `_plain`, timestamp or old schema changes. If that cannot be achieved within the two paths, save the exact source-level reason and stop the scope expansion for ROOT.
+5. Save before/after sources and restricted semantic diff in a new R103 implementation directory. Preserve ROOT finding/snapshots, all R100/R101/R102 originals, old27 RED and stop reports. Any unrelated issue is recorded for ROOT; no opportunistic repair or new product scope.
+
+## Existing32 cases, no new RED or denominator
+
+Strengthen assertions inside existing nodes only:
+
+- `test_all_p5_categories_use_same_original_owner[marker]`: actual marker consumer with fully frozen nested reference and live exact scope reaches its expected positive; descriptor/source mutation and expiry retain rejection. This is not satisfied solely by calling `_json`.
+- `test_window_export_preserves_typed_boundary_constraints`: normal dict/list vs recursively frozen Mapping/tuple canonical bytes equal; frozen VisualEvidence reference passes the same live descriptor check; mutated ID/budget/original constraint fails. Within this same node, bounded malformed examples cover integer fields set to bool, fractional counter, NaN/Infinity, non-string key, unsupported object/cycle, wrong inclusive/exclusive flag and inconsistent derived endpoint. Do not add parametrized nodes or loosen assertions to suit output.
+- `test_public_replay_descriptor_never_live_authority`: immutable and JSON-roundtrip representations work in bootstrap/supervision new-field historical decoding, while outside/revoked owner or forged new transition remains denied. Add explicit no-operational-field legacy canonical-byte/digest comparison using existing frozen originals or independently computed old codec, not a new expected value copied from the changed implementation.
+
+Reuse the approved R101 scope/remaining proof/static/GREEN; no test/reproducer/import now. Author final `R102/implementation/stop-final/budget.json` SHA256 `6c920a22ff6d345c8b206cf608844f88e76f47fc7561cdcc88531e88bee24a03` confirms RED used1/remaining0, proof0, Ruff/format/GREEN each0 used/1 remaining, formatter/mypy/collect-only/actual/Git0, no validation command in flight. Original GREEN32 P5 cases plus actual OC1 denominator and original argv/output path stay unchanged. No standalone codec probe, collect-only or new RED is granted. Keep the existing scoped proof budget; this plan grants no repeat proof. `source-semantic-after` is an earlier draft, not a proven formatting baseline: preserve it and compare the appropriate actual frozen before/after states rather than claiming AST identity across known comprehension renames.
+
+## Activation and acceptance
+
+Final author stop artifacts have arrived and were independently checked: source-freeze SHA256 `2f13baf05801477c36e64daab7c4cbe16db2e4714bacb6e8cda8288702dc28f7`, report `5e918d4bdecf24706e443d3165abdad777d69b4e36b4742fbcc96e5b75750122`, chronology `c27d48e4dd63802bf75baf437a1bc8a440a87734747c7b46910b0b9c0785bfaa`. All ten current files equal their final snapshots and pinned sizes/hashes. ROOT must revalidate these finite inputs and record activation before Sol resumes. Original R101 GREEN leaf and basetemp are absent per final budget; confirm exact leaves again before using the unchanged single command. Do not require already populated old implementation directories to be absent or overwrite stop files. A changed state outside the same codec issue requires renewed review.
+
+Then implement only this correction, continue original P5 obligations, run only genuinely remaining approved proof/static/GREEN once, and obtain different-author review. Acceptance requires legal immutable representation working through real consumer, strict malformed typed descriptors rejected, no live authority from public/history, legacy canonical bytes unchanged, exact32-case denominator and preserved original evidence. Codec completion is software evidence only; P5 startup/seven-consumer/lifecycle whole deliverable and P6/actual remain distinct gates. This plan is not a P5 PASS or actual/Git authorization.
