+# R104 — R103 activation version reconciliation
+
+Actual planner gpt-6-astra. Metadata-only plan; sole implementation author remains original GPT-6.1-sol. R103 is now frozen; do not rewrite its two plan files or any prior activation/stop record. This round changes no product, test, budget or acceptance requirement.
+
+## Actual issue and evidence
+
+ROOT activated the earlier R103 plan in tool `4e40d8`: MD SHA256 `542379513931fbd77d3388fae00efc4054a402f88507db40ab4dd3984ecb52e4`, JSON `a59d2e77e3a9ee45c1c68cc0a369b2bab81511a38e1ba8b4f1102da071eb1afc`. In parallel, planner interpreted ROOT's “two files” wording as a scope restriction, announced that interpretation and tool `e9369d` replaced the plans before receiving the later instruction to freeze them. The replacement restricted four optional adapter paths to read-only; it kept the two core paths, evidence requirements and budgets. This was a coordination/version mismatch, not a product failure.
