+# P5 operational-window software delivery — 2026-10-08
+
+P5 software has passed different-author review and ROOT acceptance. The worker creates the original operational clock/startup authority before reset and settling, hands it off once, and preserves original task/verification bounds across bootstrap, capture, planning, grounding, supervision, conditions and marker consumption. AGE is closed at its permitted boundary; hard deadlines remain strict. Public/replayed descriptions do not grant live authority.
+
+The accepted CPU evidence combines R107 29, R110 2 and R111 1 disjoint passing P5 nodes: 32 unique nodes. R111 runs two separate software worker lifecycles to verify budget change and source-file drift independently. The original 60 OC1 passes are separately reused with unchanged inputs. This is not a newly executed32/92-node batch. Original failures are preserved.
+
+This delivery includes nine production modules, one test module, three DEVELOPMENT_ONLY marker fixtures and the two frozen legacy codec files the test actually reads. The marker gzip expands to the original diagnostic frame bytes; it does not establish new actual/source qualification. The selected plans, logs, JUnit and review records are a finite evidence subset, not a complete remote raw/CPU/database reproduction package. Local raw, databases and omitted audit attachments remain local.
+
+P6 real D lease/heartbeat, transaction/publication/dispatch and backend closure is still pending. External UTC vetoes remain independent. No new physical run, native full-action qualification or formal research acceptance is claimed here. Other T12 tasks retain their existing requirements and status.
+
+Acceptance: `artifacts/research/process/20261004-ced-development/t12-sol-handoff-20261007/p5-final-acceptance-round111.md/json`. The finite R112 manifest governs this export. Candidate checkout verification and commit/push results are recorded locally after this frozen scope is prepared.
